cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MEMBRANE in academic or technical work, please cite this
  software using the metadata in this file.
title: >-
  MEMBRANE: Adaptive KV-Cache Planning for llama.cpp
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Altıntaş
    given-names: Kadir Eren
repository-code: "https://github.com/kadireren7/membrane"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-08-13"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  MEMBRANE is an open-source llama.cpp runtime layer for KV-cache
  precision and CPU/GPU residency planning under constrained memory. It
  plans GPU layer offload, whole-cache Q8/Q5/adaptive KV precision, and
  static CPU/GPU KV residency before generation, with plan-only
  diagnostics and machine-readable JSON output, on CPU and Vulkan
  backends. This citation targets the latest stable release, v0.2.0;
  the repository's main branch may contain development changes beyond
  it. Archived experiments, negative results, and benchmark/FPGA/CXL
  simulation provenance live in the companion repository
  kadireren7/membrane-research.
keywords:
  - llama.cpp
  - LLM
  - KV cache
  - inference
  - memory management
  - Vulkan
  - quantization
  - GPU offload
